vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "[tool: todowrite]\n[tool: bash]\nDelegating the search/members investigation to a subagent while I handle the rest.\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: task]\n[tool: todowrite]\n[tool: bash]\nApplying all fixes:\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: todowrite]\nThe whole suite now passes: `python3 -m unittest` reports 16 tests OK. I didn't change any tests. The first run showed 15 tests because `test_search.py` couldn't even be imported, which counted as a single error; with that fixed, both of its tests run.\n\nI gave the `test_search` and `test_members` failures to a subagent to investigate, fixed the rest myself, and tracked the work in the todo list.\n\nFixes in `catalog/`:\n- **`books.py`**: `parse_book` now turns the year into a number instead of leaving it as text. This fixes both the year test and the book-age test.\n- **`factory.py`**: added the missing third sample book, `Emma` (Austen, 1815, 1 copy).\n- **`fees.py`**: the late fee was adding the daily rate to the number of days; it now multiplies them.\n- **`inventory.py`**: `recent(n)` was returning one event too many; it now returns the last `n`. I also made it return an empty list when `n` is 0 or less. No test covers that case, but without it `recent(0)` would return the entire history.\n- **`members.py`**: raised the borrowing limit from 3 to 5, which matches the tests and the comment in the file.\n- **`search.py`**: the import pointed at a module that doesn't exist; it now imports `normalize` from `catalog.text`.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 0, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled": null, "requests_cache_read": 68457, "requests_cache_write": 74182, "requests_cost_usd": 0.45106139999999995, "requests_count": 8, "request